# WatchWave — Product Requirements Document (PRD)

> **Version:** 1.0  
> **Date:** March 29, 2026  
> **Author:** Auto-generated from codebase analysis  
> **Repository:** [github.com/subasis16/WatchWave](https://github.com/subasis16/WatchWave)

---

## 1. Executive Summary

**WatchWave** is a premium, cinematic streaming web application that delivers movies, series, and anime content through a visually rich, dark-themed interface. The platform combines real-time collaborative watch parties, offline downloads, social features, clip creation tools, and AI-powered recommendations into a single immersive experience. It targets entertainment enthusiasts who demand a high-end, Netflix-inspired streaming UI with modern social-first features.

---

## 2. Product Vision & Goals

| Dimension | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Vision** | To be the most visually immersive and socially connected streaming platform for cinematic content. |
| **Target Audience** | Movie & anime enthusiasts, social watchers, content curators aged 16–35. |
| **Core Value Prop** | Cinema-grade streaming + real-time watch parties + offline vault + community clips—all wrapped in a premium glassmorphism UI. |

### Key Business Goals
1. Deliver a production-ready streaming MVP with monetization via subscription tiers
2. Enable social engagement through real-time watch parties and friend systems
3. Provide offline-first capabilities for mobile/unreliable network scenarios
4. Build community engagement via user-generated clips and reactions

---

## 3. Technical Architecture

### 3.1 System Overview

```mermaid
