## 4. Feature Specifications

### 4.1 Authentication & User Management

| Feature | Description | Status |
|---------|-------------|--------|
| Firebase Auth | Email/password and Google OAuth sign-in | ✅ Implemented |
| User Profile | Avatar upload (compressed JPEG), editable bio, online status | ✅ Implemented |
| Profile Lock | Optional PIN-based profile protection | ✅ Implemented |
| Session Management | `onAuthStateChanged` listener + automatic redirect for unauthenticated users | ✅ Implemented |

**User Data Model (Firestore `users` collection):**
```
{
  name: string,
  email: string,
  avatar: string (base64 JPEG, max ~100KB),
  bio: string (max 150 chars),
  isOnline: boolean,
  language: "English" | "Hindi" | "Spanish" | ...,
  subtitles: "Off" | "English" | "Hindi" | ...,
  lastActive: ISO timestamp,
  badges: array
}
```

---

### 4.2 Content Browsing & Discovery

#### 4.2.1 Home Page
- **Hero Carousel:** Auto-rotating (8s interval) cinematic banner featuring 4 spotlight titles with backdrop images from TMDB
- **Content Rows:** Horizontally scrollable carousels for "Now Trending," "Absolute Classics," "Anime World," "Bingeworthy Series," and "Bollywood Hits"
- **CTA Banner:** Promotional call-to-action section in footer area

#### 4.2.2 Category Pages

| Page | Content Rows |
|------|-------------|
| **Movies** (`/movies`) | New Releases, Hollywood Action, Bollywood Hits, Crime Fiction, Dark Thrillers |
| **Series** (`/series`) | New Releases, Indian Originals, Hollywood Action, Crime & Investigation, Hit Comedies |
| **Anime** (`/anime`) | High-Octane Action, Psychological Thrillers, Super Power Sagas, Intense Sports, Heartfelt Romance |

#### 4.2.3 Movie Modal
- Triggered on content card click from any `ContentRow`
- Displays: poster image (TMDB original), title, match %, year, genres, description
- Actions: **Watch Now** (navigates to `/watch/:id`), **Download** (saves to IndexedDB with progress bar)
- Download resolves video URL from: local data → Firestore `movies` collection → fallback

#### 4.2.4 Content Data
- Static content arrays defined in `client/src/data/content.js`
- Includes metadata: `id`, `title`, `image` (TMDB poster URL), `trailerUrl`, `videoUrl`, `match`, `year`, `genre`
- TMDB API integration on the backend for dynamic content enrichment

---

### 4.3 Video Playback

#### 4.3.1 Player Page (`/watch/:id`)
- Full-featured video player using **ReactPlayer**
- Supports: Cloudinary-hosted MP4 files, YouTube URLs, YouTube-nocookie embed URLs
- Fallback: trailer URL → poster image with play/pause overlay
- Video URL resolution: local `videoUrl` → Firestore lookup → `trailerUrl` conversion

#### 4.3.2 Video Player Page (`/player/:id`)
- Alternative lightweight player entry point
- Used by Hero carousel's "Watch" button

---

### 4.4 Watch Party System

> **The flagship social feature of WatchWave.**

#### 4.4.1 Party Hub (`/party`)
- Room creation with auto-generated 6-character alphanumeric room code
- Backend stores room data (in-memory for local dev, Firestore for production)
- Room features: password protection, participant tracking, host designation
- Once live: share transmission key (room link), navigate to room

#### 4.4.2 Watch Room (`/room/:id`)
- **Real-time synchronized playback** via Socket.IO:
  - `sync_play` / `sync_pause` / `sync_seek` — Playback state sync
  - `sync_content` — Content change broadcast
- **Mood-Based Content Selection:** 6 mood categories (Happy, Sad, Relaxed, Excited, Romantic, Thriller) that filter content recommendations based on keyword matching
- **Live Chat:** Real-time messaging between room participants
- **Floating Reactions:** Heart, ThumbsUp, Laugh, Fire — animated overlay reactions
- **Role System:** Host vs. Viewer roles with toggleable controls
- **Room Settings (Host Only):**
  - Media gain control (volume sync)
  - Voice chat volume
  - Global mute toggle
  - Room moderation/report functionality
- **Share Modal:** Copy room link or invite friends directly
- **Knock-to-Enter:** Entry request system — host can accept/decline join requests
- **Voice Chat:** Microphone toggle with `getUserMedia` API

#### 4.4.3 Social Sidebar
- Visible in Party Hub alongside the main stage
- Friend list, social interactions

#### 4.4.4 Socket.IO Events

| Event | Direction | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `join_watch_room` | Client → Server | Join a room with userId and username |
| `leave_watch_room` | Client → Server | Leave a room |
| `sync_play` / `sync_pause` / `sync_seek` | Bidirectional | Playback synchronization |
| `sync_content` | Bidirectional | Content change broadcast |
| `room_message` | Bidirectional | Chat messages |
| `send_reaction` / `receive_reaction` | Bidirectional | Floating emoji reactions |
| `entry-request` / `entry-accepted` / `entry-declined` | Bidirectional | Knock-to-enter system |
| `join_chat` / `send_message` / `receive_message` | Bidirectional | Private 1-on-1 chat |
| `join_user_room` | Client → Server | Join personal notification room |
| `broadcast_notification` | Server → All | Admin broadcast notifications |
| `user-status-change` | Server → All | Online/offline status changes |

---

### 4.5 Clips System (`/clips`)

- **Community Clips Feed:** Grid of 9:16 aspect ratio clip cards (TikTok/Reel-style)
- Each clip shows: title, creator, views, likes, duration, poster image
- **Clip Creator Tool:**
  - Source video selection
  - Trim range slider (start/end seconds)
  - Tab system: Trim, Text (captions), Audio
  - Live preview with ReactPlayer
  - "Post to Community" action with encoding simulation

---

### 4.6 Offline Downloads System

#### 4.6.1 Download Flow
1. User clicks **Download** on Movie Modal or Hero
2. `resolveVideoUrl()` fetches best available video URL
3. `saveVideo()` in `offlineStorage.js` fetches the video blob
4. Video blob + metadata stored in **IndexedDB** via `localforage`
5. Progress callback updates UI in real-time

#### 4.6.2 Downloads Page (`/downloads`)
- Lists all offline-saved content with poster, title, size, download date
- Storage allocation tracker (used/total GB)
- Per-item actions: **Play Offline**, **Delete**

#### 4.6.3 Offline Player (`/offline`)
- Dedicated player that reads video blob from IndexedDB by item ID
- Completely functional without network connectivity

