## 9. Data Flow Diagrams

### 9.1 Watch Party Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Host
    participant Server
    participant Guest

    Host->>Server: POST /api/party/create (room_code, token)
    Server-->>Host: { success: true, room_code }
    Host->>Server: Socket: join_watch_room
    Host->>Host: Share room link

    Guest->>Server: POST /api/party/join (room_code, token)
    Server-->>Guest: { success: true }
    Guest->>Server: Socket: entry-request
    Server->>Host: Socket: receive-entry-request
    Host->>Server: Socket: entry-accepted
    Server->>Guest: Socket: entry-accepted

    Guest->>Server: Socket: join_watch_room
    Host->>Server: Socket: sync_content (movie)
    Server->>Guest: Socket: sync_content (movie)
    Host->>Server: Socket: sync_play
    Server->>Guest: Socket: sync_play
```

### 9.2 Offline Download Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Modal as Movie Modal
    participant Storage as offlineStorage.js
    participant IDB as IndexedDB

    User->>Modal: Click Download
    Modal->>Modal: resolveVideoUrl()
    Modal->>Storage: saveVideo(movie, url, onProgress)
    Storage->>Storage: fetch(url) as blob
    Storage-->>Modal: onProgress(percent)
    Storage->>IDB: localforage.setItem(id, {blob, metadata})
    Storage-->>Modal: success = true
    Modal->>User: "Ready for offline playback!"
```

---

## 10. Non-Functional Requirements

| Category | Requirement |
|----------|-------------|
| **Performance** | Hero images preloaded, lazy content rows, optimized avatar compression (500px max, 80% JPEG) |
| **Security** | Firebase token auth, rate limiting, Helmet headers, CORS whitelist, admin role verification |
| **Accessibility** | High contrast mode, motion reduction toggle, audio descriptions, subtitle support (7 languages) |
| **Wellbeing** | Daily watch time tracker, configurable quota threshold, weekly usage visualization |
| **Offline** | Full video download & playback via IndexedDB, service worker capable |
| **Responsiveness** | Mobile-first design, fluid typography, collapsible navigation |
| **Real-time** | Sub-second latency for playback sync, chat, reactions via WebSockets |

---

## 11. Known Limitations & Future Considerations

### Current Limitations
- Content data is primarily static (hardcoded arrays in `data/content.js`)
- Watch party room data uses in-memory storage in local dev (no persistence across server restarts)
- Firebase Admin requires `serviceAccountKey.json` for full functionality; local dev uses JWT fallback
- Clip creation is UI-only (no server-side video processing pipeline)
- Voice chat in watch rooms is microphone-access only (no WebRTC peer-to-peer audio streaming)
- Download functionality requires Cloudinary-hosted videos (YouTube URLs are not downloadable)

### Future Roadmap Candidates
- Server-side video transcoding and adaptive bitrate streaming (HLS/DASH)
- Real WebRTC voice/video chat in watch parties
- Machine learning-based personalized recommendations (beyond Gemini prompts)
- Content management system (CMS) for admin content upload
- Push notifications via Firebase Cloud Messaging
- Progressive Web App (PWA) with service worker caching
- Multi-profile support per account
- Watch history and "Continue Watching" row
- Social features: user reviews, ratings, watchlists
- CDN distribution for global low-latency streaming

